# H6 (soft; the eight-seat quad smoke rule needs concurrent8_steady, so it runs first): the stall shape of a COLD 253,920-token arrival at eight seats on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w1 (the stack, audits off), the best pack's H4 shape: the target is 8 x 262k, copied from T9e of tp4/w1-jobs: seven decoding 4k users
# (ignore_eos, 6,000-token budgets) and one cold arrival once every seat has streamed 12 chunks, with BOTH quads running. The smaller pool (four full windows instead of five) changes what the reservation admission holds, so
# the arrival is the case to run here. READ: every stream completes, the arrival has a time to first token, every seat has a recorded longest inter-token gap from the arrival on (c2_smoke_check STALL rules), no
# watchdog or replay-deadline exit, no fallback. The numbers are the owner's to weigh against the 75 tokens a second a seat is aimed at: one cold 262k prefill holds the gate, not a fault. Duration (estimate): 60 min. Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/262k8 eight-seat 262k development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/262k8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4/w1-best-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/262k8 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w1-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w1
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,stall8_cold262k
